Third-party code
----------------
Foundry vendors no third-party libraries. It is plain C11 plus, where
explicitly enabled at build time, the platform's own vendor SDKs -- CUDA
(USE_CUDA=1), Metal (USE_METAL=1), and a BLAS implementation such as Apple
Accelerate or OpenBLAS (USE_BLAS=1). Those are linked, not redistributed, and
remain under their own licenses. Rebuilding the Tenstorrent device images needs
the SFPI compiler (https://github.com/tenstorrent/sfpi); some tools and tests
call python3, curl or a llama.cpp build at run time. None of these is bundled.

Portions of the following files are derived from third-party work:

  tt/tests/test_dma_vs_pio.c
    ft_tt_dma_h2d() is transliterated from BlackholeDmaTransfer::h2d_transfer
    in tt-umd (https://github.com/tenstorrent/tt-umd), modified.

    tt-umd is (c) Tenstorrent AI ULC and licensed under the Apache License,
    Version 2.0 (LICENSES/Apache-2.0.txt).

  Other formerly Tenstorrent-derived files in tt/ were replaced in a 2026-10
  clean-room; the provenance record is docs/cleanroom/tt/README.md.

  tt/tests/test_dma_vs_pio.c also declares, locally, the struct layout of the
    tt-kmd ALLOCATE_DMA_BUF ioctl (https://github.com/tenstorrent/tt-kmd,
    GPL-2.0). Only the kernel interface layout is matched, so the program can
    call the driver; no tt-kmd source code is included. Test file only.

  barswap/k80_quirk/k80-strap-quirk.c
    Copyright (C) 2026 David (Corey) Herrera. The BAR1 resource-shrink fixup
    is modelled on quirk_s3_64M in the Linux kernel's drivers/pci/quirks.c
    (https://www.kernel.org/, GPL-2.0), modified. It is built into a Linux
    kernel, and only with the GPL-2.0 kernel. The GNU General Public License,
    version 2, is in LICENSES/GPL-2.0.txt.

  metal/kernels/fm_kernel_matvec_q4_k.{h,m}, fm_kernel_matvec_q5_k.{h,m},
  fm_kernel_matvec_q6_k.{h,m}, fm_kernel_matvec_q8_0.{h,m},
  cuda_kernels/fused_layer.cu, cuda_kernels/moe_expert_group.cu,
  cuda_kernels/matvec_q3k.cu (and their PTX in cuda/fc_cuda_ptx.h),
  and the k-quant block repack (fc_repack_*) in cuda/fc_cuda.c
    The k-quant and Q8_0 block decoding and matvec structure are modelled on
    ggml (https://github.com/ggml-org/ggml), Copyright (c) 2023-2026 The ggml
